{
  "slug": "browserless",
  "name": "Browserless",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin that gives Claude direct access to the Browserless.io REST APIs: scrape webpages, take screenshots, generate PDFs, search the web, map site structures, and run custom browser automation, all from natural language.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **9 skills**, **1 hook** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (9): `agent` (Drive an interactive browser session — navigate, snapshot the page, click, type, scroll, handle logins, captchas, cookie banners,…), `auth` (Configure Browserless API authentication), `crawl` (Crawl a website starting from a seed URL, following links to configurable depth while scraping all discovered pages), `export` (Export a webpage or file in its native format, optionally bundling all resources (CSS, JS, images) into a…), `function` (Execute custom Puppeteer JavaScript code on the Browserless cloud), `map` (Discover and map all URLs on a website using the Browserless map API), `performance` (Run a Lighthouse performance audit on a webpage and get scores for accessibility, best practices, performance, PWA, and…), `search` (Search the web using the Browserless search API), and 1 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `browserless`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install browserless@claude-community` from `browserless/claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
